# Alpha OS — Cinnamon 6.4.13 desktop — Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (resolute)
# Provenance: names verified as exact matches against the resolute
# binary-amd64 Packages indexes on archive.ubuntu.com (released 23 Apr 2026).
#
# Verified from Contents-amd64.gz: `cinnamon-common` ships BOTH
#   xsessions/cinnamon.desktop
#   xsessions/cinnamon2d.desktop
#   wayland-sessions/cinnamon-wayland.desktop   (experimental)
# so both display servers come from this single package — no separate
# X11/Wayland package split is needed.
# The session file is `cinnamon.desktop`, NOT `Xcinnamon.desktop`.
# Spices are built in as of 6.4; `cinnamon-spices*` do not exist in resolute.
# `xreader`/`xviewer` are gone — use `evince` and `eog` (shipped by nemo's
# recommendation set and listed here).
# `xdg-desktop-portal-xapp` hard-Depends on `xapps-common`, which is why
# `xapps-common` is listed explicitly alongside `libxapp1`.

cinnamon
cinnamon-common
cinnamon-control-center
cinnamon-desktop-data
cinnamon-desktop-environment
cinnamon-l10n
cinnamon-screensaver
cinnamon-session
cinnamon-settings-daemon
nemo
nemo-fileroller
nemo-python
libxapp1
xapps-common
evince
eog
xdg-desktop-portal-xapp
lightdm
lightdm-gtk-greeter
firefox
libreoffice
vlc
gnome-terminal
system-config-printer
